---
title: "push_to_backup_repo (Daily DB Backup Workflow)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_gen_filename: FILENAME = date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H-%M-%SZ .dump.gpg
    q_gen_filename --> q_clone: git clone https://x-access-token:BACKUP_REPO_TOKEN@github.com/BACKUP_REPO.git backup-repo
    q_clone --> q_copy: cp backup.dump.gpg backup-repo/FILENAME
    q_copy --> q_config: git config user.email and user.name
    q_config --> q_add: git add FILENAME
    q_add --> q_commit: git commit -m backup: FILENAME
    q_commit --> q_push: git push
    q_push --> [*]: encrypted backup pushed to remote

    note right of q_clone
        INV-001: BACKUP_REPO_TOKEN used as x-access-token for HTTPS clone authentication
        INV-002: BACKUP_REPO name sourced from secrets, not hardcoded
    end note

    note right of q_gen_filename
        INV-003: filename uses UTC ISO-8601 timestamp for lexicographic sort ordering
        INV-004: each backup file has a unique name based on execution time
    end note

    note right of q_push
        INV-005: only one file (FILENAME) is added per commit, no other files modified
    end note
